# DarwinBoot monitor-core CPU_ON launch (M3P, blob v1) as revised by
# M3P2 (blob v2, architectural-timer cadence), M3Q (blob v3,
# PROG-mailbox polling), M3Q2 (blob v3.1, ablation), M3Q3 (blob
# v3.2, x19 mailbox-pointer fix), M3R (blob v3.3, mailbox-line
# `dc civac` restored on the corrected address), M3T (blob
# v3.4: civac retired again in favour of a reader-side `dc ivac`
# beta negative control on the mailbox line, plus SIG_A/SIG_B
# signature slots at args+0x880/0x888 painted on row-3 idx2/idx3;
# see patches/m3t-coherence-sig.md) and M3U (blob v3.5: the
# monitor joins the coherency domain -- DarwinBoot allocates four
# 4 KiB page-table pages with AllocatePages and passes their base
# PA through the slot-page cell at +0x110 (PA 0x89B00110); the
# blob builds identity-mapped tables, loads MAIR/TCR/TTBR0 and
# sets SCTLR M|C|I before the v3.4 body, minus the retired ivac;
# allocation failure degrades to a GOP-painted black idx0 and no
# launch; see the v3.5 section of
# patches/monitor-core-m3p.md) and M3U2 (blob v3.5.2: the slot-page
# L3 entry 0x743 -> 0x703 -- AP[2:1]=01 made the code page EL0-writable,
# which the ARM ARM forces to PXN at EL1, so v3.5 instruction-aborted on
# its first fetch after SCTLR.M; plus row-3 idx4 stage markers S1..S4
# painted through the preamble; DarwinBoot cleans+invalidates the table
# pages before CPU_ON and paints idx4 purple on allocation failure; see
# the M3U2 section of patches/monitor-core-m3p.md and tools/m3u/) and
# M3V (blob v3.6: trace strip -- the monitor draws every ID the kernel's
# trace stubs append to the ring at args+0x980 as a sequence of colour
# cells above row 1; DarwinBoot zeroes the ring before CPU_ON; see
# patches/m3v-trace.md and tools/m3v/):
# M3Z3 (blob v3.7: same-boot EXC readout -- the monitor redraws the M3E
# crumb at args+0x800 as 6 rows x 32 bit-cells at y 2380..2670 whenever
# both magics match; see patches/m3v-trace.md):
# unified diff of the product-tree DarwinBoot.c, M3M baseline -> M3V. The firmware delta across
# revisions is the monitor section only.
--- a/DarwinBoot.c
+++ b/DarwinBoot.c
@@ -125,6 +125,329 @@
   MmioWrite32 (M3K_WDT_EN, 1);
   MmioWrite32 (M3K_WDT_RST, 1);
   (VOID)MmioRead32 (M3K_WDT_EN);
+}
+
+//
+// flashlm M3P (UniXNU-flashlm patches/monitor-core-m3p.md): monitor-core
+// launch -- DarwinBoot copies a 1872-byte position-independent blob to
+// the BootShim reserved slot page at +0x400 (offsets +0x00 x0, +0x08/+0x10
+// earliest-copy and +0x100 SLT probe are the page's other users) and
+// starts CPU7 on it with a PSCI CPU_ON SMC. The target MPIDR 0x700 is
+// CPU7's /cpus reg value in the flashlm ADT (devices.py cpu_regs,
+// confirmed from the live FDT; PSCI takes the MPIDR itself). The SMC
+// result is drawn at DiagDraw row 11 and the hand-off proceeds
+// regardless of the outcome -- a rejected CPU_ON must never block the
+// boot. The launch sits after the M3K watchdog arming (see the call
+// site): if the SMC itself never returned, the armed dog still bites
+// and recovers the device.
+//
+// flashlm M3U2: the blob (v3.5.2) enables its own MMU and data cache and
+// reads the PROG mailbox through a Normal Write-Back Inner-Shareable
+// identity mapping, joining the coherency domain the caches-off
+// readers of M3P..M3T stood outside. Its four page-table pages are
+// allocated here, immediately before the launch: the first page's PA
+// is written to the slot-page cell at +0x110 (that offset audited
+// free: the page's only users are +0x00/+0x08/+0x10, +0x100 and the
+// blob at +0x400) and the cell's cache line is cleaned next to the
+// blob copy, so the woken core -- which reads the cell with its
+// caches still off -- sees the value in DRAM. If the allocation
+// fails, the monitor is NOT launched: DarwinBoot paints the row-3
+// idx0 block black itself (a defined "no monitor" readout, distinct
+// from a fossil), reports the sentinel 0xFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF in place
+// of the CPU_ON result, and the hand-off proceeds either way.
+//
+#define M3P_MONITOR_RESIDENT  0x89B00400
+#define M3P_PSCI_CPU_ON       0xC4000003
+#define M3P_TARGET_MPIDR      0x700
+#define M3U_TABLE_PA_CELL     0x89B00110
+#define M3U_TABLE_PAGES       4
+#define M3V_TRACE_RING_PA     0xC1F14980
+#define M3V_TRACE_RING_SIZE   0x80
